        "evidence": "Proof read in full and re-derived. The two peels are correct: in H_{j+1} the rightmost generator is sigma_j and sigma_i lies in H_j, so tr^{H_{j+1}}(sigma_i sigma_j) = z tr^{H_j}(sigma_i); Markov closure then drops to H_{i+2}, where sigma_i is rightmost, giving z tr(1) = z; hence z^2. The adjacency-independence argument is also right \u2014 a length-2 word invokes no braid relation, and both stated conditions are indeed independent of |i-j|. All ten trap categories clean."
